WEBVTT

00:00:00.413 --> 00:00:03.172
Lolly turns your rules - colours, type,

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:06.182
layouts, logic - into tools anyone can use

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:09.856
to make finished files: images, PDF'S,

00:00:09.917 --> 00:00:12.566
social cards, video, by filling in a few

00:00:12.654 --> 00:00:13.819
fields.

00:00:14.592 --> 00:00:16.991
There's little to learn and nothing to

00:00:17.054 --> 00:00:20.288
upload: making and exporting runs on your

00:00:20.349 --> 00:00:22.894
device, online or off.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:27.443
This is the one page to read first.

00:00:28.207 --> 00:00:31.030
Two things get you productive: make Lolly

00:00:31.095 --> 00:00:33.538
yours and bring in what you already have

00:00:33.598 --> 00:00:36.395
«your design files and tokens».

00:00:37.169 --> 00:00:40.394
Everything else is a link away.

00:00:41.183 --> 00:00:43.664
New to Lolly and just want to make

00:00:43.726 --> 00:00:44.894
something?

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:48.171
Make something in 60 seconds walks you

00:00:48.262 --> 00:00:51.348
through three, or open the app, pick any

00:00:51.421 --> 00:00:53.893
tool from the gallery, fill in the blanks

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.644
and hit Export.

00:00:56.402 --> 00:00:58.740
Come back here when you want it wearing

00:00:58.802 --> 00:01:00.219
your brand.

00:01:01.362 --> 00:01:02.330
1.

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:05.823
Make it yours - configure your Design

00:01:05.886 --> 00:01:06.845
System

00:01:07.782 --> 00:01:10.094
Your brand in Lolly is a small

00:01:10.155 --> 00:01:13.273
design-tokens document - colours, fonts

00:01:13.349 --> 00:01:16.074
and a few rules - that every tool renders

00:01:16.134 --> 00:01:17.344
against.

00:01:18.116 --> 00:01:20.583
Set it once and everything you make is

00:01:20.659 --> 00:01:24.420
on-brand by construction, not by review.

00:01:25.199 --> 00:01:28.091
There are three ways in; pick the one that

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:31.418
matches where your brand already lives.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:35.306
Start from scratch «the design system

00:01:35.399 --> 00:01:36.331
builder»

00:01:37.361 --> 00:01:40.107
First run drops you on the gallery, with a

00:01:40.212 --> 00:01:42.375
short welcome dialog over it offering

00:01:42.465 --> 00:01:44.422
three ways in - Make it yours «the Brand

00:01:44.479 --> 00:01:47.417
Studio at #/start», Bring your design

00:01:47.472 --> 00:01:50.617
«drop a Figma, Penpot, InDesign or PDF

00:01:50.676 --> 00:01:53.352
file and it opens as an editable layout -

00:01:53.395 --> 00:01:55.588
the fastest route to Bring in what you

00:01:55.671 --> 00:01:57.570
already have below» and Explore the

00:01:57.629 --> 00:02:00.840
community tools - plus a row of languages

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:02.970
if English isn't yours.

00:02:03.733 --> 00:02:06.547
Take the first card and you land in the

00:02:06.609 --> 00:02:08.294
Brand Studio.

00:02:09.059 --> 00:02:11.772
Give it a name and a primary colour and

00:02:11.832 --> 00:02:14.664
Lolly derives a complete, accessible

00:02:14.725 --> 00:02:18.156
palette from it - light/dark surfaces,

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.978
text, accents - using the same colour

00:02:21.038 --> 00:02:24.295
maths the engine uses everywhere else.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:28.128
Pick a font, and you have a working brand

00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:29.919
in under a minute.

00:02:30.703 --> 00:02:32.734
From there the studio's six rooms -

00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:36.145
Overview, Colours, Type, Logos, Tokens,

00:02:36.226 --> 00:02:38.761
Files - let you take it as far as you

00:02:38.815 --> 00:02:41.853
like, in any order, refining any of it

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:43.820
whenever you come back.

00:02:44.585 --> 00:02:47.897
The dashboard's Design system tab «#/d»

00:02:48.013 --> 00:02:50.768
shows the result read-only and points back

00:02:50.802 --> 00:02:54.178
at #/start, which is where the editing

00:02:54.239 --> 00:02:56.668
happens «unless you're on a brand-locked

00:02:56.728 --> 00:02:59.717
build of Lolly, where the brand is fixed

00:02:59.763 --> 00:03:02.245
and there's nothing to change».

00:03:03.387 --> 00:03:06.419
Import a brand you already have

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:10.016
If your brand is already captured as

00:03:10.077 --> 00:03:13.947
design tokens - from Penpot, Tokens Studio

00:03:14.039 --> 00:03:17.914
«Figma» or any plain DTCG file - bring it

00:03:17.975 --> 00:03:21.244
in wholesale rather than retyping it.

00:03:22.018 --> 00:03:23.469
Two routes:

00:03:24.229 --> 00:03:26.942
In the app: the design system builder:

00:03:27.005 --> 00:03:29.967
Brand Studio «#/start» takes it through

00:03:30.053 --> 00:03:31.369
Add from…

00:03:32.129 --> 00:03:34.711
at the foot of its room rail - a token

00:03:34.802 --> 00:03:38.613
file, a Penpot export, an SVG or a

00:03:38.674 --> 00:03:40.394
LollyBrand pack.

00:03:41.165 --> 00:03:44.469
Drop it in and the palette lights up.

00:03:45.245 --> 00:03:47.931
From the command line, to stand up a

00:03:47.993 --> 00:03:50.069
reusable brand pack:

00:03:50.847 --> 00:03:53.668
Code example omitted.

00:03:54.433 --> 00:03:57.500
ingest:brand accepts all three containers

00:03:57.574 --> 00:04:01.142
Penpot / Tokens Studio export the same

00:04:01.202 --> 00:04:04.622
document in - a single tokens-json, a

00:04:04.681 --> 00:04:08.674
directory «$metadata-json + per-set files»

00:04:08.772 --> 00:04:11.520
or a project-penpot archive.

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:15.368
With --activate it registers the brand as

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:18.886
a profile, switches to it and rebuilds the

00:04:18.948 --> 00:04:20.294
catalog.

00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:24.253
See Configuration for how brand packs and

00:04:24.315 --> 00:04:26.519
profiles fit together.

00:04:27.643 --> 00:04:29.855
Tune it in the app

00:04:30.869 --> 00:04:34.023
Once a brand is active, keep shaping it in

00:04:34.061 --> 00:04:37.438
the Brand Studio «#/start» - change a

00:04:37.508 --> 00:04:40.376
colour or a role and every preview across

00:04:40.437 --> 00:04:43.169
the app updates as you type.

00:04:43.936 --> 00:04:47.486
«The dashboard's Design system tab at #/d

00:04:47.589 --> 00:04:50.891
shows the brand read-only; the Studio is

00:04:50.952 --> 00:04:52.744
where you edit it.»

00:04:53.501 --> 00:04:55.806
The same brand is summarised on the

00:04:55.866 --> 00:04:59.145
Profile → Your brand card.

00:04:59.922 --> 00:05:03.027
Fonts are real: pick from Google Fonts and

00:05:03.087 --> 00:05:06.152
Lolly stores the file on your device as a

00:05:06.212 --> 00:05:09.368
brand asset, so your typography travels

00:05:09.455 --> 00:05:11.923
offline and nothing is fetched at render

00:05:11.986 --> 00:05:13.095
time.

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:16.576
When you're happy, export the brand as a

00:05:16.637 --> 00:05:19.480
LollyBrand pack - a single file a

00:05:19.555 --> 00:05:22.293
colleague can import to get the exact same

00:05:22.353 --> 00:05:24.745
palette, fonts and rules.

00:05:25.504 --> 00:05:28.205
That's how a brand moves between people

00:05:28.294 --> 00:05:31.067
and machines without a server in the

00:05:31.128 --> 00:05:32.095
middle.

00:05:32.859 --> 00:05:36.294
Brand tokens round-trip both ways.

00:05:37.044 --> 00:05:40.317
Because Lolly's brand is DTCG tokens - the

00:05:40.409 --> 00:05:43.569
format Penpot reads and writes natively

00:05:43.646 --> 00:05:46.346
and Tokens Studio brings to Figma - the

00:05:46.406 --> 00:05:49.131
palette you design with and the palette

00:05:49.191 --> 00:05:52.335
Lolly enforces are one document, not two

00:05:52.394 --> 00:05:55.120
lists you keep in sync by hand.

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:58.418
See Design Tokens.

00:05:59.557 --> 00:06:00.531
2.

00:06:01.333 --> 00:06:04.130
Bring in what you already have

00:06:05.177 --> 00:06:08.469
You don't start from a blank page.

00:06:09.264 --> 00:06:12.365
Lolly opens the design work and the open

00:06:12.458 --> 00:06:14.919
formats you already own.

00:06:16.052 --> 00:06:18.963
Open-source design files

00:06:19.911 --> 00:06:22.260
Finished work in Figma, Penpot,

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:26.065
Illustrator, InDesign or any SVG app

00:06:26.125 --> 00:06:28.550
doesn't have to stay locked in the app you

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:29.970
drew it in.

00:06:30.732 --> 00:06:34.178
Open Design, click Import a design, and

00:06:34.215 --> 00:06:37.541
the file opens as a living layout - not a

00:06:37.617 --> 00:06:39.244
flattened picture.

00:06:40.015 --> 00:06:43.598
Every layer becomes an editable box: text

00:06:43.641 --> 00:06:46.741
stays retypable, shapes stay shapes,

00:06:46.805 --> 00:06:49.651
images land in your library and complex

00:06:49.712 --> 00:06:52.694
vector art is preserved faithfully.

00:06:53.445 --> 00:06:56.375
It arrives already conformed to your brand

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:58.744
faces and colour rules.

00:06:59.512 --> 00:07:02.342
The whole import happens on your device -

00:07:02.398 --> 00:07:05.224
the file is parsed in your browser and

00:07:05.287 --> 00:07:07.244
nothing is uploaded.

00:07:08.026 --> 00:07:10.720
Full details, and exactly what carries

00:07:10.786 --> 00:07:14.069
over, are in Import a design.

00:07:14.855 --> 00:07:18.118
Got a PowerPoint deck instead?

00:07:18.904 --> 00:07:20.250
Drop the .

00:07:21.077 --> 00:07:24.601
pptx on any upload surface to file its

00:07:24.667 --> 00:07:27.976
slides as assets, write a new deck from

00:07:28.037 --> 00:07:31.111
Markdown in Markdown Slides, or run

00:07:31.171 --> 00:07:33.507
Rebrand to get the same deck back

00:07:33.573 --> 00:07:37.594
re-themed, charts and animations intact.

00:07:38.729 --> 00:07:41.674
From a one-off to a template

00:07:42.643 --> 00:07:45.844
Here's the payoff: an imported layout is

00:07:45.905 --> 00:07:48.633
an ordinary Design session, so once you

00:07:48.722 --> 00:07:52.144
save it, it lives at a URL.

00:07:52.905 --> 00:07:55.955
Anyone with Lolly can open that URL,

00:07:56.019 --> 00:07:59.170
change the words, swap an image and render

00:07:59.229 --> 00:08:02.104
their own version - no design app, and the

00:08:02.164 --> 00:08:04.270
locked parts stay locked.

00:08:05.057 --> 00:08:09.792
A once-off design becomes a reusable tool.

00:08:10.564 --> 00:08:13.293
That's the whole idea, reached without

00:08:13.355 --> 00:08:16.444
writing a line of configuration.

00:08:17.582 --> 00:08:20.796
Open data and open tools

00:08:21.736 --> 00:08:24.622
The community tool set is open source and

00:08:24.683 --> 00:08:28.311
brand-agnostic - QR codes, street maps,

00:08:28.393 --> 00:08:31.265
filters, privacy utilities - and it

00:08:31.325 --> 00:08:33.849
renders against your brand the moment you

00:08:33.929 --> 00:08:35.470
activate it.

00:08:36.249 --> 00:08:39.675
Feed tools your own open data too: paste

00:08:39.714 --> 00:08:43.716
or drop a CSV or JSON table and a tool's

00:08:43.774 --> 00:08:46.422
repeating fields fill from it, one

00:08:46.515 --> 00:08:48.795
finished asset per row.

00:08:49.931 --> 00:08:51.013
3.

00:08:51.832 --> 00:08:55.256
Make something, then share or automate it

00:08:56.208 --> 00:08:59.071
With a brand active and your material in

00:08:59.133 --> 00:09:03.319
hand, every tool produces a finished file:

00:09:04.087 --> 00:09:08.399
Render any tool to SVG, PDF, PNG,

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:11.798
JPG, WebP, video and more - at true print

00:09:11.873 --> 00:09:14.236
sizes and physical units when you need

00:09:14.295 --> 00:09:15.195
them.

00:09:15.985 --> 00:09:18.844
See Exporting & formats.

00:09:19.649 --> 00:09:21.369
Share a link.

00:09:22.127 --> 00:09:25.824
Every tool state is a URL, so a finished

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:27.790
asset is reproducible and

00:09:27.850 --> 00:09:30.464
parameter-addressable - commit the link,

00:09:30.528 --> 00:09:32.870
regenerate on demand.

00:09:33.658 --> 00:09:35.818
Do it in bulk.

00:09:36.592 --> 00:09:39.481
Drive a template from a spreadsheet in the

00:09:39.542 --> 00:09:43.344
batch grid: one finished asset per row.

00:09:44.130 --> 00:09:45.868
Automate it.

00:09:46.629 --> 00:09:49.552
The same render runs from the CLI and from

00:09:49.622 --> 00:09:54.195
an AI agent - a URL is the API.

00:09:54.935 --> 00:09:59.018
"A URL is the API" is literal.

00:09:59.787 --> 00:10:03.182
The chart below was not drawn by anyone:

00:10:03.246 --> 00:10:06.187
its type, its heading and its whole data

00:10:06.249 --> 00:10:09.285
table were typed into the address bar, and

00:10:09.324 --> 00:10:11.892
the same link renders the same chart on

00:10:11.951 --> 00:10:13.470
any device.

00:10:14.609 --> 00:10:16.672
Where to go next

00:10:17.702 --> 00:10:20.150
Three pathways, depending on what you're

00:10:20.213 --> 00:10:21.843
here to do:

00:10:22.641 --> 00:10:25.994
Lolly for Creators - you make things.

00:10:26.759 --> 00:10:29.752
The advantages, and how to get the most

00:10:29.812 --> 00:10:31.420
out of the app.

00:10:32.212 --> 00:10:34.997
Lolly for Builders - you author tools,

00:10:35.057 --> 00:10:37.269
integrate and deploy.

00:10:38.051 --> 00:10:41.094
The technical documentation.

00:10:41.895 --> 00:10:44.742
Lolly for Operators - you're responsible

00:10:44.836 --> 00:10:48.523
for brand, security and rollout across an

00:10:48.585 --> 00:10:50.344
organisation.
